1
00:00:00,760 --> 00:00:04,390
130/80. That's a little high.

2
00:00:04,806 --> 00:00:08,646
(Sheldon:)We can attribute that to the stress
of sneaking past the security desk.

3
00:00:09,060 --> 00:00:11,600
(Steph:)Where did you get the stethoscope
and pressure cuff?

4
00:00:11,771 --> 00:00:14,521
(Sheldon:)My Aunt Marion gave them to me
for my 12th birthday.

5
00:00:16,109 --> 00:00:20,409
(Sheldon:)She thought if I failed at theoretical physics
that I should have a trade to fall back on.

6
00:00:21,865 --> 00:00:25,205
(Sheldon:)And by the way, the blood pressure cuff
is called a sphygmomanometer.

7
00:00:25,869 --> 00:00:28,789
(Leonard:)- Thank you.
- Didn't teach you that in medical school?

8
00:00:30,373 --> 00:00:32,163
- I'm kind of busy here.
- I understand.

9
00:00:32,334 --> 00:00:35,124
(Sheldon:)All I need is for you to authorize
these tests.

10
00:00:35,295 --> 00:00:39,595
Ha. A cardiac stress test,
a full-body MRI, an electromyogram...

11
00:00:39,758 --> 00:00:41,888
(Steph:)...a CBC, baseline glucose, upper GI?

12
00:00:42,052 --> 00:00:45,222
Oh, and exploratory laparoscopy.
The last time I had hiccups...

13
00:00:45,388 --> 00:00:48,308
(Sheldon:)...it felt like my diaphragm
was just going through the motions.

14
00:00:49,059 --> 00:00:50,979
(Steph:)Go home, Sheldon.

15
00:00:51,144 --> 00:00:52,934
(Sheldon:)Can I at least have the upper GI?

16
00:00:53,730 --> 00:00:56,110
(Sheldon:)I already drank the barium.

17
00:00:58,485 --> 00:00:59,565
(Penny:)Oh, hey.

